      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Unless the actual world has a ceiling, the big avatars that I have seen usually render completely in open spaces.\n\nSo maybe your avatar is just unnecessarily huge which might not be ideal for public areas, so my suggestion while this isn't changed, would be to either reduce the size, or show it to your friends in specific worlds that allow it or make your own world.\n\nYou could also alert some world owners about it and see if they would find your reasons good enough to update their worlds.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-08-24T10:01:22.810Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Most people who make worlds don't even know the setting exists and leave it at default, which means that no mater how infinitely big your skybox is, you're limited to a 1500m sphere.\nThis is especially annoying for people who like to make big, impressive set-piece avatars. Like a Star Wars battle or a spaceship armada. It ends up not being visible in 99% of all worlds, all because of a single variable.",
